  "articleBody": "It's frustrating when your renovation plans are stuck in permit limbo. One of the biggest reasons for delays is often incomplete or incorrect documentation. The authority having jurisdiction (AHJ) needs precise plans, calculations, and supporting documents that clearly outline your project scope. If something's missing or unclear, they'll kick it back, and that means more waiting. Another common hang-up is not knowing the specific requirements for your local jurisdiction, which can vary even within the greater Denver area. Some areas might have unique rules about what needs to be submitted, or even how fees are paid. Sometimes, folks just miss a crucial step in the application process, like forgetting to include certain product approvals or not properly addressing previous comments. Keeping track of all these moving parts can be a real headache. If your permit application seems to be stalled, it's wise to review all your submitted documents against the specific requirements, and make sure you're following up through the correct channels. Don't let your dream renovation get sidetracked by easily avoidable errors. When in doubt, or if you're dealing with multiple permits or jurisdictions, it's smart to get a professional involved to help coordinate and keep things on track.",
